      "type": "intro",
      "text": "Concurrency, Threading, and Async Architecture\nPython handles concurrent processing through distinct approaches tailored to CPU-bound or I/O-bound workloads. The Global Interpreter Lock limits true multithreaded parallelism, making multiprocessing essential for CPU-heavy tasks. Asyncio delivers high-performance non-blocking I/O using a single-threaded event loop and async-await syntax. Selecting the appropriate concurrency strategy ensures optimal throughput for high-scale network services.",
